## Donut Chart

The layer-matrix **Donut Chart** element: a self-contained SVG donut with no chart library. `@segments` ({label, value, color}[]) plus optional `@centerValue`, `@centerLabel`, and `@formatValue`. Renders proportional stroke arcs, a center figure, and a swatch legend with per-segment counts and percentages.

```gts
import { DonutChart, type DonutSegment } from '../donut-chart';

<DonutChart
  @segments={{this.tierSegments}}
  @centerValue='177'
  @centerLabel='counted'
/>
```

**The block does not know what a tier or a category is.** Segments arrive labeled and colored by the consumer; zero-value segments are dropped from arcs and legend so an empty category never renders a 0% sliver. The Matrix Tracker feeds it evidence-tier composition; any consumer with a part-of-whole breakdown can feed it something else.

Arcs are plain `stroke-dasharray` circles — no path math, no animation dependency — so the component renders identically in prerender and live contexts.

**Non-goals:** interactivity (no hover tooltips or click-to-filter — the consumer owns filtering UI), multiple rings, and percentage-label placement inside arcs at small sizes.
